   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing by tracing the peptide backbone residue by residue. Stereochemistry is only partly checked: I assumed L-configuration for most residues, and the stereocentre on the trimethylammonium \u03b2-amino acid is a guess.\n\n**Backbone, N-terminus to C-terminus:**\n- Ureido-Arg: an H\u2082N\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH cap on arginine.\n- Pen: a penicillamine, one half of the disulfide.\n- Asn.\n- Thr.\n- Trp with a 7-methylindol-2-yl side chain.\n- Lys(Ac).\n- Pen: the other half of the disulfide. The macrocycle runs from the first Pen through Asn, Thr, Trp and Lys(Ac) to this second Pen, closed by the S\u2013S bond.\n- Tyr, with its phenol O-alkylated by CH\u2082CH\u2082NH\u2082.\n- 2-Nal: 2-naphthylalanine.\n- A 4-aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid residue.\n- Lys, whose side-chain amine is acylated as described below.\n- Asn.\n- 3-Pyridylalanine.\n- N-methylglycine (sarcosine).\n- Orn, as the C-terminal primary amide.\n\n**Substituents:**\n- The Lys side chain carries a succinyl group, which is amide-linked to a \u03b2-amino acid bearing CH\u2082COOH and CH\u2082N\u207a(CH\u2083)\u2083.\n- The Orn side-chain amine carries a linker of two \u2013NHC(=O)CH\u2082O(CH\u2082)\u2082O(CH\u2082)\u2082\u2013 units, then \u03b3-Glu.\n- The \u03b3-Glu nitrogen is acylated by a C20 diacid.\n\nThe C20 chain length is an estimate. I got it by measuring the length of the zigzag in the drawing, so it could be off by a carbon or two.\n\nSMILES: NC(=O)N[C@@H](CCCNC(=N)N)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)S%10)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2[nH]c3c(C)cccc3c2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)S%10)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(OCCN)cc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc3ccccc3c2)C(=O)NC2(CCOCC2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(=O)CCC(=O)N[C@H](CC(O)=O)C[N+](C)(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2cccnc2)C(=O)N(C)CC(=O)N[C@@H](CCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@H](NC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC(O)=O)C(O)=O)C(N)=O"
